WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.322
Crunchmap reads the schedules in your syllabi and shows,

00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:07.755
before the term starts, which weeks will pile up.

00:00:07.755 --> 00:00:11.397
This is a made-up spring semester with four courses,

00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:16.160
each schedule written the way a different instructor might write it.

00:00:17.163 --> 00:00:19.196
The hardest week is week sixteen.

00:00:19.196 --> 00:00:21.044
A project and a paper are due,

00:00:21.044 --> 00:00:25.478
and last-minute work for three exams the following week lands there too.

00:00:25.478 --> 00:00:30.283
Done at the last minute, that week takes about seventy-three and a half hours.

00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:34.851
Crunchmap then plans backwards from every deadline.

00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:40.933
Each item starts as late as it can without any day going over four hours of coursework.

00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:44.079
The busiest week drops to twenty-eight hours,

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:47.365
and the busiest day from sixteen hours to four.

00:00:48.368 --> 00:00:51.567
Pick any week to see what is due and what to work on.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.921
Week eight has three exams and a paper.

00:00:53.921 --> 00:00:57.060
At the last minute that is thirty-six hours of work;

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.648
with the plan it is sixteen, because part of it moves into the weeks before.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.004
These fourteen items need an earlier start than usual.

00:01:06.004 --> 00:01:09.048
The team project's final submission, for example,

00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:13.210
starts on April third, four weeks earlier than a last-minute start.

00:01:14.213 --> 00:01:16.343
Everything comes from pasted text.

00:01:16.343 --> 00:01:19.226
This table lists every deadline that was read,

00:01:19.226 --> 00:01:22.046
with the line it came from, ready to correct.

00:01:22.046 --> 00:01:26.244
A weight comes from that line, from the course's grading breakdown,

00:01:26.244 --> 00:01:30.693
or, when neither gives one, from a typical value marked as an estimate.

00:01:31.695 --> 00:01:35.479
Finally, one file adds every deadline to your calendar,

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:40.295
plus a reminder on the morning each early or bigger item should start.

00:01:40.295 --> 00:01:45.455
Crunchmap runs entirely in your browser, and nothing you paste is uploaded.
